cid='CLM-6117-EX-001';claim={'claim_id':cid,'objective_ids':[oid],'text':'Amount in mol equals concentration in mol/dm³ multiplied by solution volume in dm³; convert cm³ to dm³ by dividing by 1000. Rearranging gives concentration = amount / volume.','claim_type':'formula','provenance':'generated_gap','evidence':[],'derived_from_claim_ids':[],'revision':1,'verification':{'status':'unverified','method':'Original structural example; arithmetic checked during build, semantic review remains required.','reviewer_id':None,'reviewed_at':None,'confidence':0.95},'publishable':False,'notes':['No official question or answer reproduced.']};save(T/'claims/canonical_claim_ledger.json',{'ledger_id':'LEDGER-6117-EX','claims':[claim]})
texts=[('formula','Choose compatible units','Concentration tells us the amount of dissolved substance in a given volume of solution. When concentration c is measured in mol/dm³ and volume V in dm³, calculate the amount n in mol using n = c × V. Rearranging the same equation gives c = n / V. Write the required quantity before choosing a rearrangement: concentration and amount are different quantities, so their units differ.'),('worked_calculation','Convert volume before substitution','A solution has concentration 0.125 mol/dm³. For a 32.0 cm³ portion, first calculate V = 32.0 / 1000 = 0.0320 dm³. Substitute into n = c × V: n = 0.125 × 0.0320 = 0.00400 mol. The concentration describes the solution; the calculated amount describes this particular portion. Using 32.0 without conversion would give an answer one thousand times too large.'),('worked_calculation','Reverse the calculation','Suppose 0.00900 mol of solute is present in 30.0 cm³ of solution. The volume is 0.0300 dm³, so c = 0.00900 / 0.0300 = 0.300 mol/dm³. Check that the denominator is the solution volume, expressed in units matching the requested concentration. Dividing the amount by 30.0 would instead give a concentration per cm³; that number cannot be labelled mol/dm³.'),('practice_guidance','Show a checkable method','For 18.0 cm³ of a 0.250 mol/dm³ solution, the conversion gives 0.0180 dm³ and multiplication gives 0.00450 mol. Show the equation, substituted values and final unit. Keep extra digits during working and round the final answer to match the supplied data. As a size check, a portion smaller than one dm³ contains less solute than one dm³ of the same solution. This check detects many volume-conversion errors.')]
